<h2>About this site</h2>
<p>I try things I'm curious about, make things, and keep a record of the process. I write about philosophy and how to live, and about the body and food, checking papers and data along the way.</p>
<p>It's a personal archive that records not only finished work, but things I'm still thinking about and things I'm still making. The site was first written in Japanese; this is the English edition.</p>

<h2>How the articles are written</h2>
<ul>
  <li>For articles on the body, food, and health, I check research papers and information from public bodies as far as I can, and cite sources in the text.</li>
  <li>I try to keep separate what research has shown, what is not yet known, and my own impressions.</li>
  <li>Health articles are general information and are not a substitute for diagnosis or treatment by a doctor.</li>
  <li>If I find an error, I check it, correct it, and note the update date on the article.</li>
  <li>English articles are translations of the Japanese originals. The numbers, sources, and claims are the same.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Advertising</h2>
<p>The Japanese edition carries advertising and affiliate links to Japanese shops, labeled "PR" or "広告" (advertisement). The English edition does not carry affiliate links. For details, see the <a href="privacy.html">privacy policy</a>.</p>
